# XCU uustat
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# uustat reports on or cancels queued uucp requests; the output format is
# unspecified and a request must exist, so the page is recorded as
# untestable.

assertion  XCU.uustat.001
anchor     utilities/uustat.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/uustat.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/uustat.html#STDOUT
class      untestable
since      1992
says       uustat writes the status of the user's uucp requests (job ID,
           user and remote system at least), and -q, -k, -r, -s and -u list
           queues, cancel, refresh or select requests.
reason     Meaningful output needs queued requests, which can only be made
           with a configured remote system, and the format is unspecified;
           cancelling or touching a job would act on the real queue.
